Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

### Motivation
- Provide upstreamable Exynos9810 SoC and Galaxy S9 (starlte) board device-tree scaffolding to enable upstream drivers (clocks/syscon/USI), power rails, storage, USB and basic user-facing peripherals.
- Replace vendor-only carveouts and add minimal reserved-memory and regulator placeholders required by UFS, panel and PMIC consumers.
- Expand pinctrl definitions with functional groups (UFS, PCIe, SD/MMC, Wi‑Fi/BT, camera MCLKs, NFC/touch IRQs) to wire board peripherals to SoC pinmux.

### Description
- Added SoC-level nodes in `arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9810.dtsi` including CMU clock controllers, syscon nodes, USI/HSI2C controller entries, UFS/UFS PHY, MMC, USB DRD, DSI/DECON stubs, sysmmu placeholders and thermal zone definitions.
- Extended pinctrl in `arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9810-pinctrl.dtsi` with many functional pin groups such as `pcie-wake`, `wlan-host-wake`, `bt-hostwake`, `ufs-rst-n`, `ufs-refclk-out`, PCIe CLKREQ/PERST, panel/camera MCLKs, SD2 pin groups and NFC/touch pin states.
- Enhanced board DTS `arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9810-starlte.dts` with reserved-memory (`ramoops`) and `cont_splash_mem`, regulator nodes (`ufs_vcc_reg`, `reg_placeholder`), PMICs (`s2dos05`, `max77705` and charger/fuel-gauge topology), touchscreen, NFC, IMU, Wi‑Fi/BT wiring, UFS/MMC pinctrl and properties, USB-C connector PD PDOs and DWC3 configuration, panel node for `samsung,s6e3ha8`, and Bluetooth device wiring.
- Added board-level pinctrl states and pin groups for keys, SD card detect (`sd2_cd`), touchscreen IRQ (`ts_int`), NFC IRQ/en/wake and panel reset.
- Added `patches/codex-analysis-report-exynos9810.md` documenting the analysis, priorities and upstreaming strategy used to produce these changes.
- Minor `.gitignore` adjustment to avoid ignoring the new `patches` report file.

### Testing
- Compiled the modified device-tree sources using the device-tree compiler (`dtc`) / `make dtbs` to validate syntax and node wiring, and the DTS files produced DTBs successfully.
- Performed basic DT structural validation (bindings/required properties) and the built DTBs did not produce errors from the compiler.
